!panic: fixedbugs2872ahandleronacoroutinesstackthatsavedinsideitselfthenleftbyajumpisrefused.answer was called after C, inside a signal handler running on a coroutine's stack (`makecontext`'s), jumped off that stack, leaving the handler's frames on it with a save point made inside them (`setjmp`, `getcontext`, `swapcontext`) that can switch back into them, so the handler was not seen to end: a handler not seen to end is held to be running, where neither this runtime's memory nor the C library's is safe to use. No function of the program is a signal handler: after `hero_net_catch_stop() -> i64` (`hero_net.h`), Ctrl-C, SIGTERM and `hero_net_ask_stop() -> ()` only make `hero_net_stop_asked() -> i64` answer 1 and a waiting call of that layer, or a mailbox's `receive` that finds it empty, answer stopped; `hero_signal_watch(sig: i32) -> i64` (`hero_os.h`) counts any other signal, and `hero_signal_take(sig: i32) -> i64` gives the count since its last call
